/bin/
/tmp/
*.test
.env
# This machine's own console login, made by `make up-data`. It holds a
# password in the clear, which is what makes it a local file and never a
# committed one.
.env.local
.brevis-sql-serve.pid
.brevis-sql-serve.log
.DS_Store
.NOTES.md
# Raw notes from the owner: a scratchpad, in Portuguese, and not a record the
# project keeps. Read against the tree it becomes a spec in docs/plan/.
NOTES.md

# Identidade visual de uma instalacao especifica. O modelo versionado e
# `brand.example.yaml`; o arquivo real e do cliente, nao do repositorio.
/brand.yaml

# go.work lets you point cmd/brevis-sdk at the local sdk while developing.
# It stays out of the repo: cmd/brevis-sdk/go.mod must require the published
# SDK, because `go install pkg@version` refuses a module carrying replace
# directives -- which is exactly how the CLI is meant to be installed.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Binários compilados dos comandos. `go build -o brevis` dentro de cmd/brevis-sdk
# deixa um de 30 MB ali, e um deles entrou no repositório na v0.4.1 e seguiu
# sendo recommitado. Artefato de build não é fonte.
/cmd/brevis-sdk/brevis-sdk
/brevis
# `go build ./...` inside sql/ leaves this one. The module was created after
# this list and nothing added it: found as an untracked 11 MB binary sitting
# in the tree, one `git add -A` from the mistake the comment above describes.
# no-binaries-check.sh does not catch it -- that gate reads what is TRACKED,
# and the whole point is that this is not, yet.
/sql/brevis-sql
/gateway/gateway
/gateway/gateway-slim

# Python build and test artefacts. `python -m build` leaves a wheel and an
# sdist in lib/python-context/dist/, `uv run` leaves a .venv and a lock, and
# pytest leaves its caches. None of it is source, and the lock in particular
# would pin a dev tool's resolution into a library that declares no
# dependencies at all.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
/lib/python-context/dist/
/lib/python-context/.venv/
/lib/python-context/uv.lock

# bench/run.sh with a local build writes the stream's dead letter here.
# Nothing should ever land in it: if something does, that IS the benchmark's
# finding, and the report says so from the gateway's own counter.
/dead-letter/

# `go build ./...` in a main package writes the binary beside the source, and
# examples/cluster/goapp is one. The image builds it in a container; the file
# here is a by-product of checking that it compiles.
/examples/cluster/goapp/goapp

# The CLI's own build output. `cmd/brevis-sdk/bravis-sdk` -- the PRE-RENAME
# name -- was swept into the rename commit of 2026-09-04 and sat in the tree
# for a month at 30 MB, against a largest legitimate file of 189 KB.
# no-binaries-check.sh is what stops the next one.
/cmd/brevis-sdk/brevis-sdk
/cmd/brevis-sdk/bravis-sdk

# The example pipeline builds its binary beside its source. Untracked, like
# the sql and gateway ones: the no-binaries gate reads what is TRACKED, so
# this is one `git add -A` away from the mistake that shipped in v0.4.1.
/examples/full-pipeline/pipeline/pipeline
